.TH FBR34KER 1 "June 2026" "FBR34KER 0.4.2b" "Developer Tools"
.SH NAME
fbr34ker \- build, validate, package, and integrate the FBR34KER monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fbr34ker
.RI [ --json ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fbr34ker
is the unified command-line interface for the FBR34KER physical-device
integration preview. It builds the freestanding ARM64 monitor and SDK,
creates deterministic FBRI bundles, validates authorized first-stage adapter
contracts, and records bounded integration evidence.
.PP
It does not include a SecureROM exploit, signature bypass, iBoot patch,
DFU-entry mechanism, or stock-iBoot-compatible Apple image.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B version
Print the release version.
.TP
.B doctor
Check compiler, linker, Python, QEMU, and optional irecovery availability.
.TP
.B build
Build monitor profiles, loader, SDK, modules, simulations, and A12/A12X/A13
FBRI bundles.
.TP
.B test
Run bounded validation. Add
.B --qemu
to execute emulator profiles when available.
.TP
.B device list
List an attached or offline recovery device and matching exact/family profiles.
.TP
.B device watch
Emit JSON events when the observed recovery device changes.
.TP
.B device doctor
Check host, device, and selected profile compatibility.

.TP
.B hardware prepare
Validate a device fixture, exact profile, and FBRI image without mutating a target.
.TP
.B hardware checklist
Print the evidence and safety checklist for a physical-validation profile.
.TP
.B hardware validate
Verify the integrity, console proof, boot evidence, and required stages in a session bundle.
.TP
.B hardware explain-failure
Explain the failed stage in a session bundle and print a bounded recovery recommendation.
.TP
.B physical-validation
Generate candidate reports or create an evidence-gated promoted profile copy.
.TP
.B bridge
Run the deterministic reference persistent first-stage bridge.
.TP
.B bringup
Run, collect, or recover an authorized adapter or bridge session.
.TP
.B session inspect
Verify evidence members and checksums.
.TP
.B session replay
Replay recorded stage and console evidence.
.TP
.B crash decode
Decode a session crash record.
.TP
.B trace timeline
Render the recorded adapter/transfer timeline.
.TP
.B boot-image
Build or inspect FBRI images.
.TP
.B ramdisk
List exact-profile targets, create an OS/build compatibility plan, build or
inspect deterministic FBRD bundles, and plan or execute loading through a
separately installed target/build-specific adapter. Loading is non-executing
by default. See
.IR docs/RAMDISK_MAKER_LOADER.md .
.TP
.B ipsw tethered-downgrade-guide
Run the guided local/download, validation, plan, external-adapter preflight,
and optional execution workflow. The target-specific adapter is not bundled;
without it the guide exits after saving a plan. The adapter is a separately
installed executable or reviewed wrapper that performs the device-side
DFU/recovery boot sequence and returns structured JSON to B34ST.
.TP
.B irecovery
Query, verify, or send through an authorized recovery session. Send is
non-executing by default.
.TP
.B deploy, recover, inspect, evidence
Invoke the bounded FBDP deployment workflow.
.TP
.B evidence-compare
Compare two bring-up evidence bundles.
.TP
.B new-board, new-driver, new-module, new-transport
Generate SDK scaffolding.
.TP
.B abi-check
Verify frozen interface versions.
.TP
.B package
Create deterministic source and complete release archives.
.SH PERSISTENT BRIDGE EXAMPLE
.nf
BRIDGE="python3 host/reference_bridge.py \\
  --state-dir build-apple/bridge \\
  --device-info examples/a13-device-info.json"

fbr34ker bringup run \\
  --state-dir build-apple/unused \\
  --device-info examples/a13-device-info.json \\
  --profile profiles/apple-a13-iphone-recovery.json \\
  --image build-apple/a13/boot.img \\
  --bridge-command "$BRIDGE" \\
  --authorized-session \\
  --authorization-id authorized-local-session \\
  --acknowledge-unsigned-code \\
  --evidence build-apple/session.zip
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I schemas/bridge-protocol-v1.json
Persistent first-stage bridge contract.
.TP
.I schemas/ramdisk-adapter-v1.json
External ramdisk loader request/response contract.
.TP
.I profiles/apple-a13-iphone-recovery.json
Exact A13 iPhone product-group profile.
.TP
.I docs/PHYSICAL_DEVICE_INTEGRATION.md
Integration workflow and evidence boundary.
.TP
.I docs/BRIDGE_PROTOCOL.md
Bridge framing, limits, operations, and security rules.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Two indicates invalid input, missing authorization, or
contract rejection. Other nonzero values indicate build, validation, transport,
or verification failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR irecovery (1),
.BR qemu-system-aarch64 (1)
